# Cloudflare Pages redirects (also honored by Netlify during migration).
# Top-down order: first match wins.
#
# Two things deliberately omitted:
#   1. Page wrappers (/landing → /landing.html, /designsystem →
#      /designsystem/index.html, etc.). Cloudflare Pages auto-handles
#      directory index and `.html` stripping, so these were redundant
#      and combined with the SPA catch-all looked like a strip-and-
#      rematch loop to its static analyzer.
#   2. SPA catch-all (/* → /index.html 200). Cloudflare Pages serves
#      /index.html for any 404 response automatically, so an explicit
#      catch-all isn't needed and itself trips cycle-detection because
#      Cloudflare strips `.html` from the destination and re-matches
#      the rule.
#
# Different-host redirects (mxqr.netlify.app → musixquare.com) live in
# netlify.toml only; Cloudflare never sees that hostname's traffic.
# Netlify also keeps the wrappers + SPA fallback in netlify.toml, so
# behavior on both hosts stays identical.

# ── Case-variant redirects → canonical lowercase (301) ──
/DESIGNSYSTEM    /designsystem/    301
/DESIGNSYSTEM/   /designsystem/    301
/DesignSystem    /designsystem/    301
/DesignSystem/   /designsystem/    301
/CHANGELOG       /changelog/       301
/CHANGELOG/      /changelog/       301
/Changelog       /changelog/       301
/Changelog/      /changelog/       301
/ROADMAP         /roadmap/         301
/ROADMAP/        /roadmap/         301
/Roadmap         /roadmap/         301
/Roadmap/        /roadmap/         301
